Maintainer: Ston Jia <ston.jia@outlook.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cmake, qt6-base-dev, qt6-tools-dev, qt6-l10n-tools, libdtk6widget-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: deepin-liferaft
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: macOS-style application-memory pressure dialog for Deepin
 Uses Fedora's systemd-oomd PSI and swap policy to open a DTK force-quit
 dialog before the kernel OOM killer acts. Applications are grouped by DDE
 app cgroup, including terminal jobs. The dialog can freeze, resume, or kill
 a selected application cgroup, and closing it resumes every frozen group.
 The user service protects its own cgroup with memory.min so the dialog
 still appears under extreme memory pressure.
 .
 The package enables kernel PSI (psi=1) on CONFIG_PSI_DEFAULT_DISABLED=y
 kernels via a GRUB snippet and enables its user service for all graphical
 sessions on install.
